 "summary": "The general results (an inducing map whose range has the homotopy extension property extends disjoint open sets, a sequential colimit is Hausdorff when its bonding maps extend disjoint open sets, a coherent increasing union is a colimit, and a colimit of cofibrations compares to such a union) are proved first, and the CW and Morse statements just specialize them. Every hypothesis is used by the lemma it feeds: T2Space by hasHomotopyExtensionProperty_range_of_coe_map_eq, IsInducing by extendsDisjointOpens_of_continuousOn.",
